+/// **(D)(iv)** The destination write carries an authorization deadline — its pre-mark's stamp plus
+/// `W_write` — and the D server's judgment of it is pinned to the millisecond: arriving one
+/// millisecond before the deadline, the write lands and is adopted; arriving AT the deadline, it
+/// is refused as expired (the comparison is inclusive), and the re-place aborts: no adoption, the
+/// pre-mark standing, the obligation queued.
+#[tokio::test]
+async fn d_iv_a_write_arriving_at_its_deadline_is_refused_and_aborts_the_re_place() {
